  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment must establish a performance baseline to anchor all subsequent comparisons. config_001 (image_only, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool) is the cleanest unimodal baseline: it uses the most widely shared image encoder (resnet50) and the simplest aggregation (avgpool), isolating the contribution of the image modality alone. This tells us (1) how well the image channel performs in isolation, (2) how multiprofile + avgpool behaves as a default pipeline, and (3) provides a reference point to later determine whether adding RNA (multimodal) or switching to a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) actually improves over a simple image-only model. Starting simple avoids conflating modality, encoder, and aggregation effects in the first data point, maximizing the interpretability of every future comparison under a tight budget."
}

